From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Subject: [PATCH] rpi-firmwared: raw property file for other drivers

Other drivers (vc4d) send whole property messages through
/scheme/rpi-firmware/property, so only rpi-firmwared uses the mailbox.
Root only. The message buffer grows to 256 words for EDID blocks.
The same interface as experiment rpi-fb's patch 0060, written for the
current driver.
---
--- a/drivers/rpi-firmwared/src/main.rs	2026-11-28 11:29:19.635174200 +0000
+++ b/drivers/rpi-firmwared/src/main.rs	2026-11-28 11:29:19.647107941 +0000
@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@
 //!   changes and time at the minimum and maximum clock (ms) of the
 //!   governor; writing `ondemand`, `performance` or
 //!   `powersave` sets the mode
+//! - `/scheme/rpi-firmware/property`: raw property messages for other
+//!   drivers (`rpi-fbd`, `vc4d`), so only this process uses the mailbox:
+//!   write a whole message (little-endian 32-bit words), read the
+//!   firmware's answer. Root only, not listed.
 //! - `/scheme/rpi-firmware/power_led`: the red power LED of the Pi 3B+,
 //!   `on` or `off`; writing sets it. It hangs on the firmware's GPIO
 //!   expander, so only the firmware can switch it. Other boards do not have
@@ -78,6 +82,8 @@
     File(Vec<u8>),
     /// A setting opened for writing, by file name.
     Setting(&'static str),
+    /// The raw property interface: the answer to the last message.
+    Property(Vec<u8>),
 }
 
 struct FirmwareScheme {
